-- The RETYPE tier: × and ≡ have an η respectively a reflection
-- principle in place of an eliminator, so the refined goal IS the
-- original judgementally and the artifact is an ascribed hole. The
-- ascription is the elimination: without it the let body would be
-- checked against the goal it always had.
def P : ℕ → 𝕌 ≔ λn. ℕ

-- one step down: the components are named, and the goal reads at them
def p : (x : ℕ × ℕ) → P (x .π₁) ≔ λx. ?g1

-- fully iterated, depth-first, intermediates kept so every let is a
-- one-step projection
def d : (x : (ℕ × ℕ) × ℕ) → P (x .π₂) ≔ λx. ?g2

-- a 𝟙 component contributes () and binds nothing
def u : (x : ℕ × 𝟙) → P (x .π₁) ≔ λx. ?g3

-- an equation binds nothing at all: what other theories build from J
-- is a change of ascription, closed by reflecting the hypothesis
def r : (a : ℕ) → (b : ℕ) → (h : a ≡ b ∈ ℕ) → P a ≔ λa. λb. λh. ?g4
